## Why This Is Asked

Assess the ability to translate usage into a cost-benefit framework for a privacy-preserving, offline-first sync feature, including storage, energy, and cloud costs.

## Key Concepts

- Data sizing and retention policies
- On-device energy and encryption overhead
- Cloud storage/egress pricing and scaling
- Privacy/compliance considerations and opt-in flows
- Go/no-go criteria and break-even analysis

## Code Example

```javascript
function estimateAnnualCost({clipsPerDay, bytesPerClip, retentionDaysCloud, users, costPerGB}) {
  const perUserMB = clipsPerDay * bytesPerClip * 365 / (1024 * 1024);
  const cloudGB = clipsPerDay * bytesPerClip * retentionDaysCloud * 365 / (1024 * 1024 * 1024);
  const monthlyCost = (cloudGB * costPerGB) / 12;
  const totalMonthly = monthlyCost * users;
  return { perUserMB, cloudGB, totalMonthly };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adjust the CBA for user growth and volatility in clip frequency?
- What privacy/consent controls would you expose, and how would they impact costs and ROI?

## Why This Is Asked
This question explores a privacy-preserving on-device machine learning use case with real-world constraints including energy efficiency, latency requirements, data minimization principles, and regulatory compliance. It emphasizes the importance of measurable go/no-go criteria and a concrete break-even timeline for implementation decisions.

## Key Concepts
- On-device machine learning models (autoencoder/isolation forest)
- Energy and performance budgeting for background tasks
- Data minimization and privacy impact assessments
- Go/No-Go criteria and break-even horizon analysis

## Code Example
```javascript
function detectAnomaly(readings, threshold){
  const mean = readings.reduce((a,b)=>a+b,0)/readings.length;
  const variance = readings.reduce((a,b)=>a+Math.pow(b-mean,2),0)/readings.length;
  return Math.abs(readings[readings.length-1] - mean) > threshold * Math.sqrt(variance);
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates practical understanding of edge caching systems, cost modeling, and operational considerations for beginner-friendly distributed systems design.

## Key Concepts

- Edge caching strategies and TTL-based invalidation
- Delta synchronization for bandwidth optimization
- Energy-aware system design for battery-powered devices
- Phased rollout planning with cohort analysis
- Offline-first architecture and fallback behavior
- Privacy, compliance, and regulatory considerations

## Code Example

```javascript
function needsRefresh(lastRefresh, ttlHours) {
  const now = Date.now();
  const ttlMs = ttlHours * 60 * 60 * 1000;
  return (now - lastRefresh) >= ttlMs;
}

function getRefreshStrategy(device) {
  const batteryLevel = device.battery ?? 100;
  const isCharging = device.isCharging ?? false;

  if (batteryLevel < 20 && !isCharging) {
    return 'defer';
  } else if (batteryLevel < 50) {
    return 'adaptive';
  }
  return 'standard';
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

